+/* the btree builder writes each leaf to the klog once, encoded and framed, with both sibling links
+ * already final: leaves are appended back to back, so a leaf's next link is its own offset plus its
+ * framed size, and the last leaf is held in memory until the builder knows whether another follows.
+ * nothing else is written to the klog until the leaves are done, which is what makes the offsets
+ * predictable. every case runs with a real codec and with none, since the two store their links in
+ * different places (the compressed block header, the plaintext leaf) */
+
